 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Lots of people do. A flexible schedule and being at home make it really easy to step away for a quick nap or errand. Think of it like training break. You come back more efficient than someone taking an hour lunch without taking breaks. Something quick that doesn't disrupt anything. A quick video or game, cup of tea, or ten minutes of reading. Agreed. A quick activity is better. Your phone will tell you how much you' actualling focusing these days. That's perfect. Little change that keeps energy up. That gives you a proper break in the middle. It feels like lunch without interrupting anything.",
